data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"researcher","content":"- CRISPR-Cas9 works by using a guide RNA that binds a specific DNA sequence, and the Cas9 enzyme then cuts the DNA at that location [3].\n- The method is adapted from a bacterial antiviral defense system and is used to modify the genomes of living organisms [7].\n- Scientists commonly use CRISPR to \"knock out\" genes by breaking them, so the cell stops making the protein they encode [2].\n- A repair template can be supplied so the cell's repair of the cut inserts a new sequence, which can replace a disease-causing mutation with a healthy one [2]."}

