data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"analyst","content":"- **Targeting mechanism:** A guide RNA binds a specific DNA sequence, and Cas9 cuts the DNA at that spot [3].\n- **Origin and reach:** The system is adapted from a bacterial antiviral defense and is used to modify the genomes of living organisms [7].\n- **Two main outcomes:** Breaking a gene stops the cell from making its protein, which is how researchers knock out genes [2]. Supplying a repair template can instead insert a healthy sequence in place of a disease-causing mutation [2]."}

